{
 "status": "final",
 "measured": "2026-09-09, definitive sweep on the 2x DGX Spark pair",
 "status_note": "Final measurement set. Two boots per arm, two runs of 100 prompts per boot, one frozen fixture, one engine build, aggregate output throughput as the headline quantity and a paired stratified bootstrap over prompts for every interval. It supersedes the 2026-09-08 single-boot set, which is preserved below as preliminary_2026_09_08 and must not be quoted as the result.",
 "baseline": "native MTP k=4. The baseline was swept (k=1/3/4/6) before the comparison was made. k=4 is the best native arm; k=3 is 0.60% behind it with a CI spanning zero, so the honest baseline is \"about 50.2 at k=3 or k=4\" and every figure here is quoted against k=4 because it is the harder number.",
 "protocol": {
  "fixture": "eval100 \u2014 100 held-out prompts, 33 code / 33 math / 34 chat, stratified from the training corpus held-out split, frozen and identical for every arm",
  "concurrency": 1,
  "max_tokens": 256,
  "ignore_eos": true,
  "temperature": 0,
  "seed": 42,
  "thinking": "off",
  "context": 8192,
  "topology": "TP2 + EP, eager, utilization 0.75 (never exceeded); the two graph-mode boots are the only non-eager arm",
  "metric_definitions": {
   "aggregate_tok_s": "sum of completion tokens over all requests / sum of wall time over all requests, counted from the final usage object",
   "median_tok_s": "median of per-request tok/s across the 100 prompts",
   "accepted_length": "engine acceptance counters: accepted draft tokens per engine pass, including the bonus token",
   "ms_per_engine_pass": "group wall time / spec draft passes; includes sampling, scheduler and IPC. Never comparable with a target-forward-only figure."
  },
  "analysis": "paired stratified bootstrap over prompts (8,000 resamples), averaging repeats within a prompt before differencing, stratified by workload; reported as a percentage difference in aggregate throughput with a conditional 95% CI. Pooled medians are NOT a paired difference test and were the source of an earlier wrong \"indistinguishable from zero\" reading.",
  "per_boot": "2 runs x 100 prompts (200 requests, 25,600 output tokens per run)",
  "boots_per_arm": 2,
  "deviation_from_brief": "The brief asked for >=5 runs x 30 prompts per boot; 2 runs x 100 prompts were run instead. The fixture is fixed-order, so --limit 30 would have measured the SAME 30 prompts every run (11 code / 10 math / 9 chat), giving per-workload intervals on 9-11 prompts. For a bootstrap that resamples PROMPTS and averages repeats within prompt, 100 prompts x 2 runs strictly dominates: 100 resampling units instead of 30, the full 33/33/34 strata, and 4 repeats per prompt across the two boots."
 },
 "boot_variance_disclosure": {
  "statement": "The intervals below are paired over prompts and contain NO boot-to-boot variance component. Two boots per arm cannot estimate one, and the observed boot-to-boot movement is the same order as the effect being reported. This is the weakest part of the result and belongs next to the numbers, not in a footnote.",
  "observed_movement": {
   "AR": "24.304 -> 25.138 (+3.4%)",
   "native MTP k=4": "50.876 -> 49.876 (-2.0%)",
   "DFlash block 4": "51.677 -> 52.186 (+1.0%)"
  },
  "headline_effect_for_comparison": "+3.87% [+2.10, +5.77]"
 },
 "thin_and_patched_arms": {
  "native MTP k=1": "ONE boot (2 runs). 18% off the pace, far outside any plausible boot variance, but do not present it as a two-boot arm.",
  "DFlash block 4": "3 runs, not 4 (its first boot contributed one run).",
  "DFlash blocks 2 and 3": "PATCHED arms. They required widening our own K allowlist in serving/plugin/dflash_epoch7.py:68 from (4,5,7) to (2,3,4,5,7). That guard is a Pixel ML scope marker, not a vLLM limit and not architectural: blocks 2 and 3 take the identical proposer path, and K < block_size (7) is already the served regime for K=4 and K=5. One line, nothing else in the file changed. The label travels with the arms."
 },
